Robert R Schneck wrote:

> DOS Prompt (called Command Prompt on recent Windowses) is the command
> line.  The "run" option is also a command line, yes.  Using "run" with
> "c:\path\to\nethack\folder\NetHackW -uwizard -D" should have the
> desired effect.

Alternatively, open your explorer and go to the NetHack directory.
Right-click on NetHackW.exe and create a shortcut.

Next, change the shortcut's properties by right-clicking on it, and edit
the command line from "NetHackW.exe" to "NetHackW.exe -uwizard -D".

Lastly, move that shortcut from the NetHack directory to your desktop by
dragging and dropping it there. You might also rename it to "NetHack
WizMode".

The advantage of this method is that you can now start NetHack in wizard
mode by double-clicking on it instead of havint to go to the command
prompt every time you want to use it.

